| `dependency_audit.fail_at` | string | `high` | one of `info`, `low`, `moderate`, `high`, `critical` (`scripts/config_loader.py` `AUDIT_SEVERITIES`) | `scripts/audit_dependencies.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `dependency_audit.fail_at` row | Sets the weakest severity `make fe-audit` fails when no accepted row covers the finding; a weaker uncovered finding is listed on stdout and does not fail. Another value is refused with exit 14. Absent, the audit writes `[using default] dependency_audit.fail_at = "high"` to stderr. | accepting one finding: `dependency_audit.accepted` | always |
